fcft.pc's own Requires.private lists tllist >= 1.0.1 (a header-only lib),
but depend= never carried it - any consumer's `pkg-config --cflags` query
that includes fcft failed *entirely* (pkgconf refuses the whole combined
query when one Requires is unresolved), silently zeroing out cflags for
every package in that query, not just fcft's own. Found chasing i3wl's
build failing on missing dbus/dbus.h and pixman.h despite both being
installed - neither was actually the problem. release=2 ships the fix.
gen-ports.py must never regenerate over this - manifest.tsv is also fixed
now, but its own template resets release=1 on every regen.

build() also unsets LD_LIBRARY_PATH now - the same LD_LIBRARY_PATH-poisoning
workaround already established for glibc-32/openrc/steam-runtime/i3wl: an
inherited LD_LIBRARY_PATH pointing into the sysroot makes even plain host
tooling (here, meson's python-exec2c dispatch) try to resolve against that
libc instead of the host's own and crash with a GLIBC_PRIVATE symbol
mismatch.

build() also passes -Ddocs=disabled - fcft's meson.build wants a real scdoc
binary (not just its pkg-config metadata) to build man pages, and no scdoc
package/recipe exists anywhere in this tree yet (foot's own makedepend
lists it too but foot has never actually been built either - same gap,
untested). Disabling docs avoids the dependency entirely since i3wl only
needs fcft's library and headers.
